WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:03.211
So, how goes it there?

00:00:03.211 --> 00:00:04.713
It's not easy being the new kid.

00:00:04.713 --> 00:00:06.297
Today I spilled soup and
hurt the most

00:00:06.297 --> 00:00:07.632
popular kid in school.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:08.883
Watch out!

00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:09.551
Curtis!

00:00:11.052 --> 00:00:11.678
I'm Ruben.

00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:15.056
You bring soup to school?

00:00:18.476 --> 00:00:20.603
I know you said I'm not supposed
to talk to you at school,

00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:22.647
but something
creepy is going on.

00:00:23.732 --> 00:00:25.608
The menu board says 
come together.

00:00:25.608 --> 00:00:26.568
I see it too.

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:27.402
It's your fault. 

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:28.653
How exactly is it my fault?

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:30.030
Guys! We all see it.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.740
Yeah, but I think 
we're the only ones. 

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:32.991
There's a logical explanation. 

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:33.742
It's a ghost.

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:36.286
Let me know if you're still

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:38.121
tired after your coffee, 
grandpa.

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:41.332
He's not your grandpa. 
He's mine.

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:43.001
Too bad. 
I don't have grandparents. 

00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:44.335
So, I've adopted him.

00:00:44.335 --> 00:00:45.837
It doesn't work that way.

00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:48.548
Is that...?

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.466
Mowgli?

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:51.676
So cool by the way.

00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:53.887
We have very different 
definitions of cool.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.222
I'm never gonna 
win this election.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.432
Will you run with me?

00:00:57.432 --> 00:00:58.349
Are you kidding?

00:00:58.349 --> 00:00:59.768
Do I look like I'm kidding?

00:00:59.768 --> 00:01:00.894
I can never tell.

00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:03.313
Hey, that's private.

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:04.439
Are you and Curtis in 
some kind of

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:06.608
secret mystery club with
Chevon and Ruben?

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:07.609
No, of course not.

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:09.986
Really? ‘Cause on 
page one it literally says 

00:01:09.986 --> 00:01:12.906
the four of you were 
chosen for a secret mystery.

00:01:13.531 --> 00:01:15.325
You have to be more careful,
Donna.

00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:16.910
We can't have people 
thinking we're running around

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.786
talking to ghosts.

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:19.788
I don't see what 
the big deal is.

00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:21.331
‘Cause you're too young 
to understand.

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:23.666
Fine, go ahead. 
Solve the mystery without me.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.336
We're completely 
out of suspects.

00:01:26.336 --> 00:01:27.462
There's no leads.

00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:28.755
I think I have an idea. 

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:31.049
Maybe we need to go to 
the scene of the crime 

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:31.758
and look around.

00:01:32.175 --> 00:01:34.677
Of course. 
It's elementary my dear.

00:01:34.677 --> 00:01:37.639
These aren't letters. 
They're elements. 

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:41.518
Potassium, sulfur, sodium, 
chlorine, and magnesium.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.228
Show off.

00:01:44.896 --> 00:01:46.272
I don't even know 
what we should do next.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:49.275
I can't believe I'm saying this 
but I'm done with this mystery.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:52.570
We can't just give up. 
The ghost wants us to help him.

00:01:52.904 --> 00:01:54.906
You were saying something?

00:01:54.906 --> 00:01:56.407
I'm pretty sure I heard you say,

00:01:56.407 --> 00:01:58.743
"Curtis was right, we 
should believe him

00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:00.620
and follow him always."

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.163
That doesn't even sound like me.

00:02:02.163 --> 00:02:03.498
Can you two focus?

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:06.251
I decided to run with 
you for student council.

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:08.253
What? Are you serious?

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:09.462
Yes. Now don't get so hyped up

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.964
or else I'm gonna 
change my mind.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:13.424
Okay. Okay. I'm calm.

00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:15.593
We need a plan.

00:02:15.593 --> 00:02:17.887
We need to get these 
characters back in the book.

00:02:18.763 --> 00:02:19.639
Woah.

00:02:20.598 --> 00:02:21.766
Responsibility?

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.852
She wants us to 
take responsibility?

00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:26.020
If anyone should take 
responsibility it's you.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:26.980
Oh really?

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.817
Children, you must not 
quarrel amongst yourselves.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.070
Forgive me for abandoning you.

00:02:34.946 --> 00:02:35.822
I forgive you.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.117
You must remain a united front.

00:02:40.034 --> 00:02:42.203
We've come this far. 
We can't give up now.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.875
When I moved here, 
I had no friends. 

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:50.545
But once I met Donna, 
Curtis, and Chevon,

00:02:50.545 --> 00:02:51.921
it changed everything.

00:02:51.921 --> 00:02:53.882
They are splendid friends.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.720
When I first met you I thought 
you were a weird comic book geek

00:02:58.720 --> 00:02:59.929
that brought soup to school. 

00:02:59.929 --> 00:03:00.889
And now?

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:03.391
At least you stopped 
bringing soup to school.

